## The 30-Day Implementation Protocol

You now have the four laws. Here's how to apply them.

### Days 1-7: Design
- Pick ONE habit
- Apply the formula: "After [CURRENT], I will [NEW]."
- Choose a 2-minute version
- Make it obvious (set up the environment)
- Make it attractive (pair with a treat)
- Make it easy (remove all friction)
- Make it satisfying (set up the tracker)

### Days 8-21: Execute
- Do the 2-minute version daily
- Don't break the chain (calendar X)
- If you miss a day, restart the next day — never miss twice
- Don't add complexity yet

### Days 22-30: Expand
- If 2 minutes is feeling easy, expand to 5 minutes
- Don't jump to 30 yet — let the identity shift first
- At day 30, review: did I do this 25+ times? ? If yes, you're forming the habit. Add a second one.

### Month 2: Layer
- Add habit #2 (use the same protocol)
- Habit #1 is now automatic. Don't touch it.
- New habits compound — but only after the first is stable

### Month 3: Identity Check
- "Am I becoming the kind of person who does this?"
- If yes, you have a real habit
- If no, the system needs adjustment — not more willpower

